    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers around capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, who presents a high xERA of 4.68. **Matt Chapman** stands as our premier play (69.71) today, fueled by a perfect storm of an elite #1 order slot, strong BvP historicals (29 PA), and a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher that creates a high-leverage environment for stolen bases. **Dylan Beavers** (66.63) and **Taylor Ward** (62.61) also project as strong starts, largely due to a massive +16% park factor adjustment in their hitter-friendly venue against Burke. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.84) rounds out the top-tier of our daily offense; his promotion to the #2 spot, combined with his elite sprint speed, makes him an essential piece in our quest to dominate the scarcity-driven SB category.\n\nOur bench decisions were primarily dictated by defensive positioning and the \"Below floor\" efficiency threshold. **Drew Gilbert** (48.26) was the closest to the cut, ultimately squeezed out of a higher projection by a brutal L/L platoon disadvantage against the starter and a bottom-of-the-order assignment. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on **Gavin Sheets** (49.91) to provide stability at 1B. While **Gavin Sheets** benefits from a minor wind-out boost, his score remains marginal; we are essentially playing him to reach the inning threshold rather than expecting a ceiling performance. \n\nRisks for the day are concentrated in our \"Lineup Pending\" designations. With the official cards not yet turned in, we are assuming aggressive batting order positions for **Cal Raleigh**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Lawrence Butler**. If these players are shuffled down in their respective lineups, their efficiency scores will see a downward correction. **Cal Raleigh** (58.30) carries the highest variance risk; while his raw power provides a solid floor, his score is contingent on maintaining that #5 spot to maximize RBI opportunities. We are holding **Daulton Varsho**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** in reserve today, preferring to keep their plate appearances fresh for upcoming matchups where platoon advantages are more pronounced.",
